{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T22:12:03.740Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 2 is implemented and both verifies pass.\n\n**What I built**\n\n`src/core/run/focused-tests.ts` exports:\n- `collectFocusedTests(projectRoot, config, scope)` — checks `traceability.focusedTests`, resolves scope with `resolveScope`, builds one import graph (skipping `config.paths.openspecRoot`) and one scenario index, then reads only `scenarioTestFiles` / `scenariosInFile` / `testsNaming` to return scoped opted-in scenario pairs and every repository scenario test file naming them (sorted, distinct). Empty when the command is unset, no capability is opted in, or no scenario is collected.\n- `runFocusedTests(collection, projectRoot, changeFolder, config)` — single-quotes each file into the `{files}` placeholder, spawns through `runVerificationCommand` with the change folder and verify timeout, and classifies TAP output as `failed` / `problem` / `passed` (failed wins; `not ok` lines parsed at any indentation, with directives stripped and `\\#` / `\\\\` unescaped). Returns `null` when nothing is run.\n\n`tests/focused-tests.test.ts` covers the four delta scenarios plus the space/quote path, escaped `\\#`, indented `not ok`, `# TODO`, timeout, and `OSQ_CHANGE`, all on temporary projects using tiny `node` TAP scripts.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/focused-tests.test.ts` → 12 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → passes (typecheck, build, full suite, biome)\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/082-traceability-fast-feedback/.run/results/2.md`."}}
